 taken","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வாளடு","parts":[{"text":"வாளடு","lemma":"வாளடு","gloss":"with a sword"}],"gloss":"with a sword","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"படு","parts":[{"text":"படு","lemma":"படு","gloss":"fall/die"}],"gloss":"fallen"},{"surface":"பிணம்","parts":[{"text":"பிணம்","lemma":"பிணம்","gloss":"corpse"}],"gloss":"corpses"},{"surface":"பெயரா","parts":[{"text":"பெயர்","lemma":"பெயர்","gloss":"move/turn over"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ஆ","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"turning over"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செங்களம்","parts":[{"text":"செம்","lemma":"செம்மை","gloss":"red"},{"text":"களம்","lemma":"களம்","gloss":"field"}],"gloss":"red battlefield"},{"surface":"துழவுவோள்","parts":[{"text":"துழவு","lemma":"துழவு","gloss":"search/stir"},{"text":"ஓள்","lemma":"அவள்","gloss":"she"}],"gloss":"she who searches"},{"surface":"சிதைந்து","parts":[{"text":"சிதைந்து","lemma":"சிதைந்து","gloss":"having been shattered"}],"gloss":"having been shattered","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வேறாகிய","parts":[{"text":"வேறு","lemma":"வேறு","gloss":"different/other"},{"text":"ஆகி","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"become"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having become severed/mutilated"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"படுமகன்","parts":[{"text":"படு","lemma":"படு","gloss":"fall/die"},{"text":"மகன்","lemma":"மகன்","gloss":"son"}],"gloss":"fallen son"},{"surface":"கிடக்கை","parts":[{"text":"கிட","lemma":"கிட","gloss":"lie"},{"text":"கை","lemma":"கை","gloss":"noun suffix"}],"gloss":"lying state"},{"surface":"காணூஉ","parts":[{"text":"காணூஉ","lemma":"காணூஉ","gloss":"having seen"}],"gloss":"having seen","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஈன்ற","parts":[{"text":"ஈன்ற","lemma":"ஈன்ற","gloss":"that gave birth"}],"gloss":"that gave birth","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஞான்றினும்","parts":[{"text":"ஞான்று","lemma":"ஞான்று","gloss":"time"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"oblique case suffix"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even/than"}],"gloss":"even than the time"},{"surface":"பெரிது","parts":[{"text":"பெரிது","lemma":"பெரிது","gloss":"greatly"}],"gloss":"greatly"},{"surface":"உவந்தனளே","parts":[{"text":"உவந்தனளே","lemma":"உவந்தனளே","gloss":"she rejoiced"}],"gloss":"she rejoiced","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Veins rising, shriveled, not fleshy, weak shoulders / of a lotus-like waist, the old woman's son / 'His army defeated, he fled,' as many said, / 'If he retreated in the raging battle, the breast that he suckled / I will cut off!' thus saying, with anger, / taking a sword, turning over the fallen corpses, / searching the red battlefield, shattered and severed / her fallen son's lying state having seen, / even more than the day she gave birth, she greatly rejoiced.","translation":"With veins standing out on her shriveled, thin, weak shoulders, and a waist like a dry lotus stalk, the old woman's son was rumored by many to have fled, defeated in battle. Enraged, she cried, 'If he indeed retreated from the raging fight, I will cut off the breast that suckled him!' Grasping a sword, she went to the blood-stained battlefield, turning over the fallen corpses. When she found her fallen son lying there, hacked to pieces, she rejoiced even more than on the day she gave birth to him.","modern":"நரம்புகள் வெளியே தெரியும்படி உலர்ந்துபோன, சதைப்பற்றற்ற மெலிந்த தோள்களையும், தாமரைத் தண்டு போன்ற இடுப்பையும் உடைய அந்த முதியவளின் மகன், போர்க்களத்தில் தன் படை தோற்றுப் பின்வாங்கி ஓடிவிட்டான் என்று பலர் கூறினர். அதைக் கேட்டுச் சினமடைந்த தாய், 'அவன் போர்க்களத்தில் அஞ்சி ஓடியிருந்தால், அவனுக்குப் பாலூட்டிய என் முலையை அறுத்து எறிவேன்' என்று சபதம் செய்தாள். கையில் வாளை ஏந்திக்கொண்டு, போர்க்களத்தில் மடிந்து கிடக்கும் பிணங்களைப் புரட்டிப் பார்த்துத் தேடினாள். அங்கே தன் மகன் உடல் சிதைந்து வீர மரணம் அடைந்து கிடப்பதைக் கண்டாள். அதைக் கண்டபோது, அவனைப் பெற்றெடுத்த நாளை விடவும் அவள் பெரிதும் மகிழ்ச்சி அடைந்தாள்.","explanation":"This is a Puram poem of the tumpai tiṇai (warfare), depicting the theme of uvakaik kaluḻcci (weeping with joy / ecstatic pride of a mother). An old, frail mother hears rumors that her only son fled from the battlefield. Outraged at the thought of raising a coward, she vows to cut off the breast that fed him. She searches the bloody battlefield, turning over corpses with a sword. When she finds her son's body hacked to pieces, proving he died facing the enemy bravely, she rejoices more than she did on the day he was born.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}